{"reference":"1 Samuel 6","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Ark Narrative","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter completes the ark narrative’s reversal of Israel’s earlier attempt to treat the ark as a guarantee of victory. The LORD’s power is shown without an Israelite army: the Philistines acknowledge his hand against their communities and return the ark. The ark is therefore not presented as an object Israel can control, but as belonging to the God who acts freely.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_006_bd19dc43fde32477625f11c9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}